Source: boswas-security
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: boswas-security
Architecture: all
Depends: apparmor, auditd, libpam-pwquality, nftables, sudo, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: apparmor-utils, unattended-upgrades
Description: Boswas OS security baseline
 Configuration package implementing the Boswas OS v1 security baseline
 with standard Debian mechanisms:
 .
  * nftables host firewall (inbound default deny), loaded through a
    nftables.service drop-in; Debian's /etc/nftables.conf is not modified
  * desktop-safe kernel hardening sysctls (user namespaces stay enabled for
    Flatpak and browser sandboxes)
  * auditd rules for identity, privilege and security configuration changes
  * bounded persistent journal retention
  * sudo defaults (no privileges granted) and password quality policy
  * restrictive sshd policy for when SSH is explicitly provisioned
  * unattended-upgrades restricted to the Debian security archive
  * USB/removable-media policy framework (not enforced in v1 alpha)
